WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:02.801
-It is lovely to meet you.
-It's lovely to meet you.

00:00:02.801 --> 00:00:03.801
-Thank you for being
on the show.

00:00:03.801 --> 00:00:05.701
It is Perm Week.

00:00:05.701 --> 00:00:08.634
I'm sure you've heard.
-And saw.

00:00:08.634 --> 00:00:11.367
-Yeah, and saw as well.
Have you ever had a perm?

00:00:11.367 --> 00:00:13.000
I think you may --
Can I guess?

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:14.734
I think you might have had one.

00:00:14.734 --> 00:00:15.767
-I...

00:00:15.767 --> 00:00:16.767
I've had a perm.

00:00:16.767 --> 00:00:18.133
-You have?
-Yeah.

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:19.334
-You're allowed to
talk about it.

00:00:19.334 --> 00:00:21.334
-It's slightly traumatic.

00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:22.501
-It is?
-It is.

00:00:22.501 --> 00:00:23.801
Well, so...

00:00:23.801 --> 00:00:25.200
I can't even believe
I'm actually --

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:28.601
I've never really told anyone
this story, but I...

00:00:28.601 --> 00:00:31.968
I was, a few years ago, going
through a very bad breakup.

00:00:31.968 --> 00:00:34.567
I'm telling this story because
what I would like to do

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:38.868
is sort of start a form
of activism against hairdressers

00:00:38.868 --> 00:00:43.400
allowing to do perms on people
who are going through a breakup.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:44.834
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.834 --> 00:00:46.767
[ Applause ]
-It's real!

00:00:46.767 --> 00:00:48.801
-It's a real thing.
-It's so real.

00:00:48.801 --> 00:00:51.501
-They should ask you before
they give you the --

00:00:51.501 --> 00:00:54.300
-I think I think there should be
a law that if you sit --

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.434
-A law?
-A law, yes.

00:00:56.434 --> 00:00:58.501
You pass loads of laws
in this country.

00:00:58.501 --> 00:01:00.334
-Yes, we do. Yes. We try.

00:01:00.334 --> 00:01:03.434
-So if you sit down in a chair
in a hair salon and you say,

00:01:03.434 --> 00:01:07.767
"Hello, I would like a perm,"
the person has to say,

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:10.367
"Are you going through
a terrible breakup?"

00:01:10.367 --> 00:01:12.367
And if you say yes,
they can't --

00:01:12.367 --> 00:01:13.667
-They ask for you to leave.

00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:15.701
-They say,
"We can give you a trim."

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:19.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:21.234
-So what exactly went down?

00:01:21.234 --> 00:01:22.667
So you went in, bad breakup.

00:01:22.667 --> 00:01:24.968
--I went in and I was
very, very sad.

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:29.133
And I think I'd seen,
like, a magazine cover

00:01:29.133 --> 00:01:31.234
and someone looking gorgeous,
and I'd said to the hairdresser

00:01:31.234 --> 00:01:33.501
who was doing my hair
for an event,

00:01:33.501 --> 00:01:35.434
"God, she looks so good.
What has she done?"

00:01:35.434 --> 00:01:36.734
And I think
this hairdresser said,

00:01:36.734 --> 00:01:37.801
"Oh, she's had a perm."

00:01:37.801 --> 00:01:39.167
And I went, oh my God.

00:01:39.167 --> 00:01:42.033
That's going to solve
all of my problems.

00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:44.234
So I went, and then she said,
which shall not be named.

00:01:44.234 --> 00:01:46.434
She said, "Go to this salon.
They're doing perms."

00:01:46.434 --> 00:01:48.100
[Clicks tongue]
"They're doing a perm."

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:49.300
And I was like,
"Great, I'll go."

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:52.033
So then I went
and got in the chair

00:01:52.033 --> 00:01:54.367
and I got this perm,

00:01:54.367 --> 00:01:56.234
which is
a very extensive process.

00:01:56.234 --> 00:01:59.100
It's like, 6 hours of regret.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:00.501
You just sit there
and you're like,

00:02:00.501 --> 00:02:02.300
"This is just so bad."

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:03.734
-And then you're at the point
of no return,

00:02:03.734 --> 00:02:05.868
at one point, and you go,
"I'm getting a perm."

00:02:05.868 --> 00:02:07.434
-There's so many
points of no return.

00:02:07.434 --> 00:02:10.033
-Many points of no return.

00:02:10.033 --> 00:02:13.834
-But my hair was, you know,
it was like straw, short.

00:02:13.834 --> 00:02:15.934
I mean,
it was already kind of snappy

00:02:15.934 --> 00:02:17.167
and it was so bad.

00:02:17.167 --> 00:02:18.601
-It was rough?
-It was so rough.

00:02:18.601 --> 00:02:21.400
Anyway, here's
the real clincher for me,

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:26.067
is that my hair
didn't do the perm-y thing.

00:02:26.067 --> 00:02:27.367
So they took the thing --

00:02:27.367 --> 00:02:29.901
Chris looked amazing, right?
-Of course. Yes.

00:02:29.901 --> 00:02:31.334
-Yes, Chris looks great.

00:02:31.334 --> 00:02:33.300
-So then when they took
the thing,

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.400
the little twizzler
thingies out,

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:41.501
it was just like the saddest,
most, like, wilted little thing.

00:02:41.501 --> 00:02:43.701
-So did you look like
an extra for,

00:02:43.701 --> 00:02:45.100
the girl from "The Ring"
or something?

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:46.701
What did you look like?

00:02:46.701 --> 00:02:47.868
-I don't even --

00:02:47.868 --> 00:02:50.667
I looked like when
I was in primary school

00:02:50.667 --> 00:02:53.567
and I thought, "I know, I'm
going to sleep in curlers."

00:02:53.567 --> 00:02:55.634
-Oh, my God.
-It was so bad.

00:02:55.634 --> 00:02:57.033
And then I remember,

00:02:57.033 --> 00:02:59.701
I walked out of the hair salon
and my phone rang,

00:02:59.701 --> 00:03:04.100
and it was my publicist,
my amazing publicist, Lisa.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:05.667
And I pick it up and she goes,

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:07.000
"Oh, hi, honey. How are you?"

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:10.133
And I said,
"Lisa, I just got a perm."

00:03:10.133 --> 00:03:13.601
And then there was
this, like, 15-second pause.

00:03:13.601 --> 00:03:15.033
And then she just said,

00:03:15.033 --> 00:03:16.901
"Oh, honey, why?"

00:03:16.901 --> 00:03:19.501
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.501 --> 00:03:21.033
It was so bad!

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:22.033
-That's a great response.

00:03:22.033 --> 00:03:25.234
"Oh, honey, why?"
-"Oh, honey, why?"

00:03:25.234 --> 00:03:26.634
The pain in her voice.

00:03:26.634 --> 00:03:29.501
And I knew she was thinking,
"When is she ever in public,

00:03:29.501 --> 00:03:31.868
like, in the next
5 to 6 months?"

00:03:31.868 --> 00:03:33.300
-Yeah, because you have to
just throw it out.

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:34.467
You don't have an option.
-Cancel, cancel.

00:03:34.467 --> 00:03:36.067
-You have to
shave all your hair off, yeah.

00:03:36.067 --> 00:03:38.434
I got to say, you are
phenomenal in "The Crown."

00:03:38.434 --> 00:03:40.667
Congratulations
on all the accolades.

00:03:40.667 --> 00:03:42.634
[ Applause ]

00:03:42.634 --> 00:03:47.200
Golden Globe, you're nominated
for two SAG Awards coming up.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.200
Congratulations on this.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.567
Do you enjoy going
to these awards shows?

00:03:51.567 --> 00:03:53.767
I do enjoy them,
but I get very nervous

00:03:53.767 --> 00:03:55.133
in rooms full of -- yeah.

00:03:55.133 --> 00:03:57.167
Well, there's like,
so many famous people.

00:03:57.167 --> 00:03:58.634
It's kind of strange, you know?

00:03:58.634 --> 00:04:00.467
And I've never been
to the Golden Globes before.

00:04:00.467 --> 00:04:01.567
I took my little sister,

00:04:01.567 --> 00:04:04.834
who is a trooper
and a very calm person.

00:04:04.834 --> 00:04:07.467
But we were super,
super jet-lagged.

00:04:07.467 --> 00:04:09.667
We'd just got in.
-Yeah.

00:04:09.667 --> 00:04:11.300
-And the next day
we were thinking about it,

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.067
because we didn't --
I didn't really meet

00:04:13.067 --> 00:04:14.901
that many people,
and I was thinking,

00:04:14.901 --> 00:04:16.167
what was I doing?

00:04:16.167 --> 00:04:18.868
And then I realized
that we basically were like,

00:04:18.868 --> 00:04:21.801
treating it like we were in
a Jane Austen novel.

00:04:21.801 --> 00:04:22.901
We didn't get up once,

00:04:22.901 --> 00:04:24.234
and everyone just
walked past our table.

00:04:24.234 --> 00:04:26.200
We sort of went,
"Thank you for coming."

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:27.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.000
And I got a text from a friend
who was watching,

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.801
like, on the television,
and she just said,

00:04:31.801 --> 00:04:35.767
"Get up
and say hi to someone."

00:04:35.767 --> 00:04:38.501
-"Say hi to someone."

00:04:38.501 --> 00:04:40.501
Did you ever see yourself
or think like,

00:04:40.501 --> 00:04:43.801
"Oh, maybe one day,
I could play Princess Diana?"

00:04:43.801 --> 00:04:45.300
-No, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:47.067
No, I never. No.

00:04:47.067 --> 00:04:49.701
I never saw a resemblance,
really, no.

00:04:49.701 --> 00:04:51.267
-Well, let me show
everyone a picture.

00:04:51.267 --> 00:04:54.033
This is you as Princess Diana

00:04:54.033 --> 00:04:56.434
and then the real
Princess Diana.

00:04:56.434 --> 00:04:57.667
[ Applause ]

00:04:57.667 --> 00:05:02.033
I mean, it's kind of insane.
It's unbelievable.

00:05:02.033 --> 00:05:05.501
That's fantastic.
-Yeah.

00:05:05.501 --> 00:05:06.767
-So you go into the audition.

00:05:06.767 --> 00:05:09.167
Did you know that you were
auditioning for Diana?

00:05:09.167 --> 00:05:10.567
-So it's a weird story.

00:05:10.567 --> 00:05:15.667
I knew in a kind of vague way
that I was going to play

00:05:15.667 --> 00:05:17.734
this part for a very --
like, five years.

00:05:17.734 --> 00:05:21.033
So I went in and I did an
audition for a part in season 2

00:05:21.033 --> 00:05:22.901
-Of "The Crown"?
-Of "The Crown."

00:05:22.901 --> 00:05:25.434
Season 1 had just come out
and it was a really big hit,

00:05:25.434 --> 00:05:27.734
and everyone was,
rightly so, very excited.

00:05:27.734 --> 00:05:31.501
My agent called me up and said,
"Just go in," and basically,

00:05:31.501 --> 00:05:34.300
I was so physically wrong
for this part.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.033
I'll never tell anyone
what it is.

00:05:36.033 --> 00:05:37.801
-Okay.
-So people's imaginations.

00:05:37.801 --> 00:05:40.067
-Does the character have a perm?

00:05:40.067 --> 00:05:41.534
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.534 --> 00:05:45.834
So I went and I did this
pretty bad audition.

00:05:45.834 --> 00:05:47.667
You know, they kind of
stopped me and they were like,

00:05:47.667 --> 00:05:50.400
"We'll call you.
Thank you so much," you know?

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:51.601
-Oh, that is the worst.
-Brutal.

00:05:51.601 --> 00:05:54.567
So then I left,
and then I got an email,

00:05:54.567 --> 00:05:56.868
this sort of ambiguous email,
the next day saying,

00:05:56.868 --> 00:06:01.801
"Definitely not that part,
but maybe Diana."

00:06:01.801 --> 00:06:02.934
But it was about, you know,

00:06:02.934 --> 00:06:05.100
it was like,
five years in the pipeline.

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:07.367
-So that means you have to wait
five years for them

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:08.968
to remember that you auditioned.

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:10.501
-I didn't really think
it was going to happen.

00:06:10.501 --> 00:06:12.067
-Yeah, usually it doesn't
happen, to be honest.

00:06:12.067 --> 00:06:13.534
-That's the thing.

00:06:13.534 --> 00:06:15.634
And then when I bring this up
with the producers and I say,

00:06:15.634 --> 00:06:17.434
you know,
it was like five years of hell,

00:06:17.434 --> 00:06:18.501
where I was like,

00:06:18.501 --> 00:06:20.701
"Please, God,
let this come along."

00:06:20.701 --> 00:06:23.501
They all say, "Oh, no.
We always knew it would be you."

00:06:23.501 --> 00:06:28.400
And I think, we? Like, we?
What we? Royal we?

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:31.167
-Me, I did not.
-No, no.

00:06:31.167 --> 00:06:32.801
-You are phenomenal in this.

00:06:32.801 --> 00:06:34.100
I want everyone
to watch "The Crown."

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:35.534
I want to show a clip right now.

00:06:35.534 --> 00:06:39.000
Here's Elizabeth Debicki
in "The Crown." Take a look.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.601
-What's this
about us going home?

00:06:41.601 --> 00:06:42.868
-It turns out there's

00:06:42.868 --> 00:06:47.000
a diary conflict
through no fault of mine,

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:48.934
and I have to get back.

00:06:48.934 --> 00:06:50.267
-We're supposed to be here
for two weeks.

00:06:50.267 --> 00:06:52.067
-Yes, I know.

00:06:52.067 --> 00:06:53.901
Plans change.

00:06:53.901 --> 00:06:55.968
I have a commitment
at Oxford University.

00:06:55.968 --> 00:06:58.667
-It isn't the university.

00:06:58.667 --> 00:07:00.100
It's a summer school
for tourists.

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:01.400
It's not essential.

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:05.167
-It is to me.

00:07:05.167 --> 00:07:07.734
-This is our holiday.

00:07:07.734 --> 00:07:09.701
It's a rare opportunity for us
to be together

00:07:09.701 --> 00:07:10.934
with the boys as a family.

00:07:10.934 --> 00:07:12.834
And I know you struggle
with that sort of thing,

00:07:12.834 --> 00:07:14.601
which is why I agreed to
you bringing your friends

00:07:14.601 --> 00:07:16.634
along to entertain you.

00:07:16.634 --> 00:07:18.901
And I even agreed
to do the photo call today

00:07:18.901 --> 00:07:20.634
requested by your people
so the lie could be

00:07:20.634 --> 00:07:21.667
paraded to the world's media

00:07:21.667 --> 00:07:23.100
about what an adoring husband
you are.

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:24.567
On one condition.
-What's that?

00:07:24.567 --> 00:07:26.968
-That you actually are one!

00:07:26.968 --> 00:07:30.400
-Ooh! Elizabeth Debicki!

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:33.534
All seasons of "The Crown"
available now on Netflix.

00:07:33.534 --> 00:07:35.834
More "Tonight Show" after
the break, everyone.

00:07:35.834 --> 00:07:39.133
Stick around. Make that a law!

